        },
        {
          "id": "doc-7d4923c19c25::sentence-5",
          "documentId": "doc-7d4923c19c25",
          "text": "The reason for the sky turning red is the way smoke particles scatter sunlight. ",
          "start": 342,
          "end": 422,
          "context": "Evidence 1: Were the skies red just because of the flames/smoke?  The reason for the sky turning red is the way smoke particles scatter sunlight.  Smoke particles are fairly large and are better at scattering the longer (red) wavelengths of light, known as Mie scattering. "
        },
